parts.part_stem:
Two balls $X$ and $Y$, of equal diameter but different masses $0.24\text{ kg}$ and $0.12\text{ kg}$ respectively, slide towards each other on a frictionless horizontal surface, as shown in Fig. 2.1.
{{figure:figure_2_1}}
Fig. 2.1

Both balls have initial speed $2.3\text{ m s}^{-1}$ before they collide with each other. Fig. 2.2 shows the variation with time $t$ of the force $F_{Y}$ exerted on ball $Y$ by ball $X$ during the collision.
{{figure:figure_2_2}}
Fig. 2.2

parts.text:
On Fig. 2.3, sketch the variation with time $t$ of the force $F_{X}$ exerted on ball $X$ by ball $Y$ during the collision in (b).
{{figure:figure_2_3}}
Fig. 2.3

